          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.279,
            0.847,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Notice how the graph is organised, what scale is used, and what patterns the data shows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.324,
            0.846,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) How would you describe the change for various states between 2022 and 2024?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.367,
            0.846,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(d) Approximately how many more registrations did Assam get in 2023 compared to 2022?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.412,
            0.847,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(e) How many times more did the registrations in West Bengal increase from 2022 to 2024?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.455,
            0.847,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(f) Is this statement correct — ‘There were very few new registrations in Uttarakhand in 2023 and 2024, as the increase in the bar lengths is minimal’?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.539,
            0.405,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.4 Data Detective"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.567,
            0.847,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We put well-formed sentences one after the other to make a beautiful story. In the same way, well-organised and well-presented data can tell interesting stories, and can also expose new mysteries or help solve mysteries!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.662,
            0.362,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Telling Tall Tales"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.688,
            0.847,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Earlier, we saw data of two Grade 5 classrooms with heights of boys and girls in each class. There, the average height of girls was more than boys in one class and vice versa in the other class."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.756,
            0.802,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Following are the dot plots of heights of boys (in blue) and girls (in orange) of Grades 6, 7 and 8 (in that order) of two different schools. What do you notice? Share your observations."
            }
          ]
        },
